 op/1/src_region/0,0,1920,1274/5571_ebbflownew1.rev.1773259197.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:26525
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/Chicago
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.tc.umn.edu/live/image/gid/517/width/80/h
 eight/80/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1920\,1274/5571_ebbflownew1.rev.17732591
 97.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-ALL-DAY:1
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Addressing the violence of separation\, the pr
 actice of keeping memories and the invasive effects of colonialism\, <str
 ong>Pritika Chowdhry</strong>\, <strong>Chotsani Elaine Dean</strong> and
  <strong>Courtney M. Leonard</strong> contemplate the past\, the present 
 and possible futures in their large scale\, ceramic-based installation wo
 rks. The individual works poetically contemplate the 1947 partition of In
 dia\, the manual and psychological labor of enslaved and free African Ame
 ricans and the changed environments and indigenous lifeways brought on by
  outside occupation and settlement.\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:Art History|Art|Exhibit|Weisman Art Museum
END:VEVENT
