SUMMARY:More Various\, More Beautiful\, and More Terrible
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;  From its origins in 1934 as the University Gallery\,
  Weisman Art Museum has been committed to collecting the work of American
  artists. Critically considering the history and nature of that commitmen
 t\, this new Woodhouse Family Gallery installation highlights the variety
  and relevance of the museum's holdings of United States art with a focus
  on the many contested terrains at play in American art\, history\, and e
 xperience.  &#160\;Find more about this exhibition\, and see a sampling o
 f artwork images\, on the Weisman's website &gt\;&gt\; (https://wam.umn.e
 du/more-various-more-beautiful-and-more-terrible)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  &#160\;</p><p>  From its origins in 193
 4 as the University Gallery\, Weisman Art Museum has been committed to co
 llecting the work of American artists. Critically considering the history
  and nature of that commitment\, this new Woodhouse Family Gallery instal
 lation highlights the variety and relevance of the museum's holdings of U
 nited States art with a focus on the many contested terrains at play in A
 merican art\, history\, and experience.</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p><a href="ht
 tps://wam.umn.edu/more-various-more-beautiful-and-more-terrible">Find mor
 e about this exhibition\, and see a sampling of artwork images\, on the W
 eisman's website &gt\;&gt\;</a></p>
