LOCATION:West Bank Skyway
GEO:44.97246;-93.243304
SUMMARY:UMN\, Farm Aid\, & Activism | West Bank Skyway
DESCRIPTION:Highlighting the 40-year history of Farm Aid (https://www.far
 maid.org/festival/)\, this exhibit led by History Professor Andrew Kobaya
 shi Deckrow (mailto:adeckrow@umn.edu) explores University of Minnesota's 
 response to the farm crisis through music\, activism\, and Minnesota-base
 d partnerships. The project compiles work from undergraduate students in 
 the History 3001: Public History course from fall of 2025\, as well as th
 e History Department's second annual History Lab in the spring of 2026.  
 All are invited to the opening reception in the West Bank Skyway on April
  29 from 2-4 p.m.  Questions? Contact Professor Andre Kobayashi Deckrow: 
 adeckrow@umn.edu (mailto:adeckrow@umn.edu)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Highlighting the 40-year history of <a 
 href="https://www.farmaid.org/festival/">Farm Aid</a>\, this exhibit led 
 by History Professor <a href="mailto:adeckrow@umn.edu">Andrew Kobayashi D
 eckrow</a> explores University of Minnesota's response to the farm crisis
  through music\, activism\, and Minnesota-based partnerships. The project
  compiles work from undergraduate students in the History 3001: Public Hi
 story course from fall of 2025\, as well as the History Department's seco
 nd annual History Lab in the spring of 2026.</p><p>  All are invited to t
 he opening reception in the West Bank Skyway on April 29 from 2-4 p.m.</p
 ><p>  Questions? Contact Professor Andre Kobayashi Deckrow: <a class="Pro
 semirrorEditor-link" href="mailto:adeckrow@umn.edu">adeckrow@umn.edu</a><
 /p>
